      "writtenOn": "2023-05-02T14:27:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a non-mutable slice.\nAlso note this is a temporary that gets dropped at the end of this function; Ciborium wants a Vec passed by value, so that seems unavoidable.\n\nThe Vec returned by value_to_bytes below is also allocated by Ciborium. I could instead use a mutable slice, if we\u0027re willing to pick a maximum size. But why?",
